File Index

/classifyMovement.ts
Purpose: Shared movement classifier + exit normalizer — MOVE_DIRS is the corpus-verified 10-token real vocabulary (n/s/e/w/ne/nw/se/sw/u/d, no long-word up/down); classifyMovement() checks a command's first token against it (used by autoleveling-engine's send/movement-wait paths); normalizeExit()/exitsToSet()/DIR_TO_COMMAND (long-form-tolerant, uppercase CompassDirection) serve the compass UI and GMCP room_data exits. Replaces useCompassBlock.ts's own normalizeExit and autoleveling-engine.ts's isMovementCommand/MOVE_DIRS.

/movementTracker.ts
Purpose: Corpus-validated shared FIFO movement tracker (35k-real-move validated, see .ai-plans-completed/closed-incomplete/20260813-1325-movement-tracking-fix.md). Listens to shatteredarchive:command-sent (enqueues on a classifyMovement hit), game:room-data ({room,sector,exits} diff = success; darkness resolves nothing and never updates last-known; an EXACT repeat while pending resolves immediately as succeeded rather than blocking — the "ambiguous-repeat" case), and shatteredarchive:raw-data (fixed failure substrings + a line-anchored door-closed regex = failure). Per-entry timeout is HEAD-OF-QUEUE-RELATIVE (1200ms since an entry became the front of the queue, re-armed on every resolve) — an absolute-from-send-time timeout was corpus-proven to misclassify 44.7% of real bursty movement as failed; head-relative drops that to 5.4%. Re-dispatches movement-attempt/-succeeded/-failed with the existing payload shape. 2026-09-12: now bound live — MainContainer.tsx calls movementTracker.bind() once at app scope (independent of any one component's mount state), and both old trackers (useCompassBlock.ts, autoleveling-engine.ts) have been migrated onto it (Steps 3/4) — neither dispatches movement-attempt/-succeeded/-failed itself anymore.

/movementTracker.ts
Purpose: Because bind() runs at app scope, its game:room-data listener also fills roomDataStore (the shared "where am I" cache). The HUD widgets that used to be the only writers (compass, room header) are not always on screen, and a window opened later (the map) found no room and stayed idle until the next move. Keep that write here: it is the one listener that is always bound. movementTracker.roomCache.test.ts drives the bound listeners through real events, a typed move needs the short direction (n, not north).

/movementTracker.ts (HEAD_TIMEOUT_MS, 2026-11-19)
Purpose: HEAD_TIMEOUT_MS is exported because the autopilot engine derives its movement backstop from it: max(idle wait, 4 x HEAD_TIMEOUT_MS) plus the allowance for commands still queued (features/autoleveling/autoleveling-engine.ts, docs/game/autopilot.md "Pause and stop"). Changing it moves the point at which a stalled move pauses the run. A pending move that is older than it is dropped by the tracker; the engine waits longer so the tracker settles first.
